 "result_text": "cpplint no longer warns about the `;` after the closing brace of a C++20 `requires` expression. The change is in `cpplint.py`.\n\nI checked it against a scratch file in `/tmp` with two concepts: your `requires(T t) { ... };` and a `requires { ... };` with no parameter list. Neither produced a `readability/braces` warning. I didn't run the repo's test suite, and I didn't add a test, per your instructions.\n\nTwo edits cover the two forms:\n- **`requires (...) {`:** the check that skips macro-like names before a `(` now also skips `requires`.\n- **`requires {`:** a new check skips any line containing `requires` followed by `{`.\n\nThe second check is a plain line match, so it also skips the warning for any other `{` on the same line as `requires {`.",
